<section class="page-hero"><img class="bg" src="/assets/img/photos/north-bennington-house.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/north-bennington-house-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/north-bennington-house.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="900" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.1"><div class="wrap"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">›</span>Claim questions</nav><span class="kicker on-dark">Answers by topic</span><h1>Vermont Insurance Claim Questions, Answered</h1><p class="lede">Plain answers grouped by topic: the basics, costs and timing, Vermont specifics, and working with us.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn gold" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn light" href="/claim-review-request/">Free claim review</a></div></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose"><div class="callout"><b>Jump to a topic:</b><ul><li><a href="#faq-1">The basics</a></li><li><a href="#faq-2">Costs and timing</a></li><li><a href="#faq-3">Vermont specifics</a></li><li><a href="#faq-4">Working with us</a></li></ul></div><h2 id="faq-1">The basics</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>What is insurance appraisal?</summary><div class="a"><p>A process written into most property policies for resolving disagreements over the amount of a covered loss. Each side names an appraiser, the appraisers choose an umpire, and an award signed by two of the three sets the amount.</p></div></details><details><summary>Who can demand appraisal?</summary><div class="a"><p>Most policies let either you or the insurer demand appraisal in writing. Some policies add conditions, so read the wording.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is appraisal the same as arbitration?</summary><div class="a"><p>They are related but not identical. Appraisal is usually limited to the amount of loss, while arbitration can address broader issues. Vermont courts look at the policy language.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does appraisal decide coverage?</summary><div class="a"><p>Generally no. If the carrier denies that the loss is covered at all, that is a coverage dispute, usually handled through a complaint to the Department of Financial Regulation or with an attorney.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="faq-2">Costs and timing</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>How much does appraisal cost?</summary><div class="a"><p>Each side pays its own appraiser and usually half the umpire. Costs depend on the size and complexity of the claim. We quote fees in writing before starting.</p></div></details><details><summary>How long does it take?</summary><div class="a"><p>Many residential appraisals finish within one to three months of the demand. Larger claims and scheduling can take longer.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is there a deadline to demand appraisal?</summary><div class="a"><p>Some policies set a time limit, and the suit-limitation clause can also affect timing. Check your policy and talk to a professional if dates are close.</p></div></details><details><summary>What if the gap is small?</summary><div class="a"><p>If the difference is small, appraisal fees may eat the recovery. A documented supplement request to the carrier is often a better first step.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="faq-3">Vermont specifics</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Who regulates insurance in Vermont?</summary><div class="a"><p>The Vermont Department of Financial Regulation, through its Insurance Division. It licenses insurers, agents and public adjusters and handles consumer complaints.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does Vermont have a FAIR plan or wind pool?</summary><div class="a"><p>Vermont does not operate a coastal wind pool. Hard-to-place risks are often written by surplus lines carriers. Check with the Department of Financial Regulation for current options.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is flood covered by a homeowners policy?</summary><div class="a"><p>Usually not. Flood from rising water is generally excluded and covered under a separate flood policy, such as the National Flood Insurance Program.</p></div></details><details><summary>Are ice dams covered?</summary><div class="a"><p>Many policies cover sudden interior water damage caused by ice dams. Some limit roof repairs or ice removal. Read the water, roof and freezing wording together.</p></div></details><details><summary>What about bad faith?</summary><div class="a"><p>Vermont recognizes claims against insurers for bad-faith handling in some circumstances, and Title 8 lists unfair claim settlement practices. We do not give legal advice; consult a Vermont attorney.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="faq-4">Working with us</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Are you a public adjuster?</summary><div class="a"><p>No. We work as appraisers, estimators and umpires. A public adjuster handles the whole claim; we focus on the amount of loss.</p></div></details><details><summary>Are you lawyers?</summary><div class="a"><p>No. We do not give legal advice. When a claim needs a lawyer, we say so.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do you work outside the big towns?</summary><div class="a"><p>Yes. We work in all 14 Vermont counties, including the Northeast Kingdom and rural southern Vermont.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can you guarantee a result?</summary><div class="a"><p>No honest appraiser can. We can promise a thorough, defensible valuation and a candid opinion about whether appraisal makes sense.</p></div></details></div></article>
<aside class="aside"><div class="box call"><h2 class="box-t">Talk it through first</h2><p>The first conversation is free. We will tell you plainly whether appraisal fits your claim.</p><a class="big" href="tel:+18445371427">+1 (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn gold" href="/claim-review-request/">Send claim details</a></div><div class="box"><h2 class="box-t">Learn</h2><ul><li><a href="/vermont-appraisal-process/">How appraisal works<span aria-hidden="true">›</span></a></li><li><a href="/vermont-claim-questions/" aria-current="page">Claim questions (FAQ)<span aria-hidden="true">›</span></a></li><li><a href="/searchable-claim-glossary/">Searchable glossary<span aria-hidden="true">›</span></a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-field-guides/">Field guides<span aria-hidden="true">›</span></a></li></ul></div></aside></div><section class="cta-band"><div class="wrap"><div><h2>Didn’t see your question?</h2><p>Call or email. We are happy to talk it through.</p></div><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn gold" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn light" href="/claim-review-request/">Email the estimate</a></div></div></section>
